<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via 7-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via 7-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve injected reserves into the banking system on Monday through seven-day system repurchase agreements, a New York Fed spokeswoman confirmed.</p>
<p>The RPs are for fixed collateral.</p>
<p>The operation was generally expected.</p>
<p>Federal funds were at their 5-1/2 percent target rate at the time of the operation.</p>
<p>((  -- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867 ))</p>
